<TextPage title={`About ${SITE.name}`} description={`Who runs ${SITE.name}, how the calculators work and how to reach us.`} h1={`About ${SITE.name}`} path="/about/">
  <p>{SITE.name} is a free collection of date and time tools for people in the United States, the United Kingdom and Canada. It answers everyday questions — “what’s the date 90 days from today?”, “how many days until Christmas?”, “how old am I exactly?” — instantly, with a calendar, a countdown and a link you can share.</p>
  <h2>Who runs this site</h2>
  <p><b>{SITE.author.name}</b> — {SITE.author.bio}</p>
  <h2>How the calculators work</h2>
  <p>Every tool uses the same tested date engine. Dates are counted on the Gregorian calendar with today as day 0, month lengths and leap years handled automatically, and business days counted Monday to Friday. Pages are rebuilt every day, and each calculator also recalculates in your browser using your device’s date, so results are right in every time zone.</p>
  <p>Holiday dates follow published rules (for example, US Thanksgiving is the fourth Thursday in November). Where a government can move a holiday — such as UK bank holidays — check the official notice for legal deadlines.</p>
  <h2>Guides</h2>
  <p>Our guides are written with AI assistance and reviewed by a person before publishing. Read the <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> for details.</p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions, corrections or ideas for a new tool? See the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
</TextPage>
